WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.885 --> 00:00:06.080
- [Mark] All right, Amado.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.260
Amado where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.180
Where are you from originally?

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.010
- [Amado] I'm from the
MacArthur Park area.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.050
- [Mark] So, L.A basically.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.350
- [Amado] Yeah, like 6th and Alvarado.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.810
Yeah, not far from here.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:18.030
- [Mark] And you had both
your parents growing up?

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.500
- No, my father, he went
to prison when I was three.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.300
My mother raised me and my brothers.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.510
- [Mark] So dad was in prison
for most of your childhood?

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:27.660
- Yeah, until he died.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.500
- [Mark] Oh, really?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.450
What was he in for?

00:00:30.998 --> 00:00:34.220
- He was there for a murder.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.950
He killed somebody.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.090
- [Mark] Was he in gangs?

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.410
- Yeah, he was a gang member.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.650
Him and my brothers were gang members.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:41.830
- [Mark] And you avoided it somehow?

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.550
- Yes, I did it because of that.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.982
Since I was so much younger,
I was able to see it

00:00:45.982 --> 00:00:46.815
from a different perspective,

00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:48.573
and decided it wasn't the life for me.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.990
- [Mark] And where did your life go

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.540
from there after you left home?

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:57.660
- I went to prison too.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.710
I used to be a lifer.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:01.640
- [Mark] What were you in prison for?

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:03.340
- I killed somebody when I was 18.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.230
He was a guy that was trying
to kill me and my friend.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.730
He ended up killing my friend.

00:01:10.077 --> 00:01:12.080
And, I ended up in the
process of defending myself,

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.230
I ended up killing him.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.370
I later on got it
overturned and I got out,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.607
but I did 11 years,
almost 12 years on that.

00:01:18.607 --> 00:01:19.907
- [Mark] But it was self-defense?

00:01:19.907 --> 00:01:21.527
- It was in self-defense, yeah.

00:01:21.527 --> 00:01:22.923
They got me for a manslaughter.

00:01:23.843 --> 00:01:25.620
That's what they got me for.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.570
There is no self-defense in California.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.750
- [Mark] No such thing?

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.110
- Well, it's what they tell you.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.820
You can't take the law
into your own hands.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.880
You have to find a police officer

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.760
or something to help you.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.663
But, I was scared.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.520
I thought he was gonna kill me for sure.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.617
And I just was trying to
fight the best I could,

00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:47.380
and I ended up overcoming him.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.580
But it was the way that it
happened that got me in trouble.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.420
After it happened, I was afraid,
and they had to catch me.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.520
So since I ran, it made me look like

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.950
I was doing something underhanded.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.560
But I was just scared.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.393
I was young, I was scared.

00:02:01.393 --> 00:02:02.570
I didn't want to do the
rest of my life in prison.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.070
- [Mark] How did you kill him?

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.370
- I killed him with an ax.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.503
In these older buildings,
there's a lot of those fire axes.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.493
The idea was when he was
chasing me through the building,

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.721
my only hope, I have to defend myself.

00:02:20.721 --> 00:02:22.803
And, I picked the ax out of the case,

00:02:24.142 --> 00:02:26.260
and it's how I killed him.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.463
It was kind of gruesome.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.073
- [Mark] So from 18 'til like 29?

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:36.783
- Yeah.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:39.883
Actually 31.

00:02:41.143 --> 00:02:41.976
I got out when I was 31.

00:02:41.976 --> 00:02:42.809
- [Mark] You've been
out for a couple years?

00:02:42.809 --> 00:02:43.642
- Yeah.

00:02:43.642 --> 00:02:46.210
That's when I got out, 31.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.547
- [Mark] Oh, you got out when you were 31?

00:02:47.547 --> 00:02:48.760
- I'm 43 now.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:49.910
- [Mark] Oh, you're 43?

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.920
So today you're living where?

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.970
You're on Skid Row?

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.166
- I'm on Skid Row.

00:02:57.166 --> 00:02:59.877
I just got back from Mexico.

00:02:59.877 --> 00:03:02.130
I had a mother who was ill,

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.106
and I went to go take care of,

00:03:04.106 --> 00:03:06.272
but she lost her battle with cancer.

00:03:06.272 --> 00:03:08.185
And, I came back, I buried her.

00:03:08.185 --> 00:03:10.050
I came back after I culminated

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.260
a relationship that I had out there.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.440
I ended up getting in a relationship

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.230
at the time I was taking care of her.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.270
But it didn't work out for us.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.853
So I decided to come back.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.715
I've been back for
about a year and a half.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.653
About a year into coming back,
I started dating somebody.

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:30.550
It just changed my life, you know?

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:31.950
I had a lot of plans before.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:37.310
I was excited about being
back and doing things again.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.083
But I mean, contracting
HIV changes everything.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.660
Well, at least what I
thought I knew about it.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:44.780
I'm starting to learn a lot more

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.160
about it now that I have it.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.670
I'm starting to look into it.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:48.650
And when I was growing up,

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.160
I mean, it was a death sentence.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.623
If they told you you had
HIV, you were going to die.

00:03:53.747 --> 00:03:57.050
And when I found out I was
like, what am I going to do?

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.510
Go to school, get a job?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.090
What's the point?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.760
So I started getting high, you know?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.733
And I've never been one to get high,

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.920
but it just seemed like the
right thing to do at the time.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.230
Now I'm transitioning even out of that.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.710
And then I'm thinking to
myself, what are you doing?

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.000
This is stupid.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.880
You have a limited amount of time.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.060
Do something with yourself.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.810
Being high is not going
to enable me to do that.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.220
I've had to concentrate,

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.603
and this is going to be
the fight of my life.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.310
From what I understand now,
I could live a normal life.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.617
If I take care of myself.

00:04:31.617 --> 00:04:33.270
And I stop killing myself with drugs,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.010
and just this lifestyle.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.340
So, I'm trying to get out of here.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.333
I was trying to take me
and my girlfriend out,

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:43.093
but she's stuck here.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.110
This is her life.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.434
She loves this.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.053
She loves something about this place.

00:04:50.788 --> 00:04:55.788
I don't feel I can save her,
so I have to save myself.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:57.560
I struggled with that in the beginning,

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.963
because I felt bad leaving her behind.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.090
I don't leave people behind to die.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.240
But, I mean, I have to do something,

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.073
otherwise I'm going to die with her,

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.393
and I can't die out here.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.560
I have to do something.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.487
- [Mark] How did you contract
AIDS in the first place?

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:17.790
- Sleeping with her.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.755
I'm thinking, I mean, I
don't know how you find out

00:05:20.755 --> 00:05:21.860
like where you get it from,

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.150
but I've never been one to sleep around.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:27.650
I made it a point to never
sleep with girls out here.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.030
And this girl approached me,

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.930
and told me she liked
me and liked my style,

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.220
and wanted to have me as a boyfriend.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.660
What did I think?

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.200
And I thought to myself,
who am I to deny her?

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.140
I know what she she did
and stuff like that.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.740
But she seemed like a nice girl.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.580
Maybe you needed a better example.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.253
So I said, okay, well, you
wanna see where this goes?

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.570
About a year into our relationship,

00:05:56.570 --> 00:06:00.497
I started seeing how she lived
and how promiscuous she was,

00:06:00.497 --> 00:06:01.917
and how she was doing it behind my back.

00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:03.300
And I started finding out that the guys

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.193
she was sleeping with,
some of these guys had HIV.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.923
So I encouraged her to go
get tested and she did.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.380
And it turns out she did have,

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:14.430
not only HIV, but a bunch of other stuff.

00:06:16.904 --> 00:06:18.510
And I didn't want to go get
tested, to get confirmed.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.560
I didn't even go get
tested for like six months.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.210
Because it shocked me when
I found out she had it.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.913
But not like when I found
out I really truly had it.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.734
And I don't know how to
describe what it's like.

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:31.634
I'm just not sure.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.900
It's even embarrassing to
tell friends and family.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:39.600
You want to tell them to help you,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.700
and you want to explain to them

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.730
what's happening in your life,

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.730
but it's hard to tell them you have HIV.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:45.913
It makes you feel dirty.

00:06:48.437 --> 00:06:49.620
I don't know, it's just hard.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:50.770
It's hard to tell them.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.680
So, it's hard to reach
out and ask for help.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.010
But I recently done
that, and it took a lot

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.240
of courage to tell them I had HIV.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.390
'Cause I know they're
going to tell other people,

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:06.893
and I'm always going to
be that guy who had AIDS.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.210
I never thought that I would be that guy.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.383
But, we'll see how it goes.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.413
It's hard.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.840
- [Mark] The medications they
have now are great, though.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:25.040
- Yeah, they can really
save your life, man.

00:07:28.608 --> 00:07:30.960
I'm barely starting to find
out still, 'cause like I said,

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.600
I'm barely starting to get into

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:33.670
the treatment and everything like that.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.590
So I don't know too much about it.

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:37.530
But I mean there's pills that,

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.690
it would basically clean
out my blood and my system

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:43.290
so well that if you test
me, I won't even come out.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.630
And I won't be able to
get my partners infected.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.910
So that means I could maybe start dating.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.240
And I could maybe have a regular life.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.240
Like maybe I could have a
wife, I've never been married.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.720
I don't have kids.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.330
Maybe I can still do that.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.950
And I thought that was not a
possibility for me anymore.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.550
And that has always been
my dream, to have a family.

00:08:06.737 --> 00:08:08.250
From what they're telling me,

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:11.370
it looks like I could
still have a normal life

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.203
if I start making the changes now,

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.543
and I do what I have to do to get better.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.620
If not, it's going to kill me.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.473
I see people out here,
how fast they deteriorate.

00:08:24.605 --> 00:08:25.438
It takes them.

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:28.592
I don't want to be taken that way.

00:08:28.592 --> 00:08:30.092
Like it took my girl's mother.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.410
She looked healthy, she looked fine.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.360
And then one day she just died.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.400
It's crazy.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:36.350
I don't want that to be me.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:38.860
So many people are dying
out here right now.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.030
It's crazy how many people are dying

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:43.290
from all kinds of different stuff.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.984
And tomorrow it could be me.

00:08:44.984 --> 00:08:46.740
They can be like, oh, remember that guy?

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.573
Yeah.

00:08:47.573 --> 00:08:48.406
Oh, he was a nice guy.

00:08:48.406 --> 00:08:49.650
Oh yeah, well he died.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:50.483
Oh, what happened?

00:08:50.483 --> 00:08:51.570
He had HIV.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:53.810
Or, he did die from an overdose.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.800
So whatever it is.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.150
I don't want that to be me.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.433
I want to do better than this.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.160
Maybe come back and
help and inspire others

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.460
to do the same thing, show
them that it can be done.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.230
'Cause there's not a lot
of people doing that.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.210
No one ever comes back

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.030
and tells you their success story.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.010
I don't ever hear anything like that.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.350
No one ever comes back and tells me,

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.270
hey man, it's possible.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:17.823
Like, this is what you can do.

00:09:18.792 --> 00:09:20.233
I think if someone came back and did that,

00:09:20.233 --> 00:09:21.943
that would help a lot of people.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:24.413
It's not over.

00:09:25.973 --> 00:09:27.553
This is only the beginning.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.380
I mean, that's the way I feel now.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.107
Now I have something to fight for.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.070
I have something to live for, not die for.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.270
- [Mark] Your attitude is great,

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:43.300
considering the tragedies
that you had to go through.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.133
- Yeah.

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:46.400
I don't have a lot of family.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.690
Like I said, I just lost my mother.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.670
She was like that last real family I had.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.953
So like, I'm alone.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.090
I mean, that's all I need, I guess.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.770
I know that if she found out I had HIV,

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.270
it would have broke her heart.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:09.013
I'm glad that she passed away
and didn't have to find out,

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.130
'cause it would have broke her heart.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.183
To find out her youngest son died of AIDS.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:16.940
'Cause she probably thought of AIDS

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.720
in the way I used to think of AIDS.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.800
- [Mark] It's changed a lot.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:20.633
- Yeah.

00:10:20.633 --> 00:10:22.363
It's not like it used to be.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:28.743
I mean there's commercials
and all kinds of stuff now.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.140
They used to make you feel
like it was dirty before.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.930
It was like only bad people got that.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:38.470
But I notice now that
anybody can catch it.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.430
It's everywhere.

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.895
If you're not careful you can get it.

00:10:41.895 --> 00:10:42.940
And you have to really be careful.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.360
I was not careful enough.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:48.780
I took it for granted and
I had unprotected sex.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:49.890
And you don't really think about it.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.690
Unprotected sex, oh,
it only takes one time.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:53.550
You don't think about that.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.730
I never really did, not
took it that seriously.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.960
Once I got to know a girl for awhile,

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:59.400
and I knew her well enough,

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.130
yeah, I can have unprotected sex with her.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:04.210
But that could have been it right there.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:06.290
Or I could maybe infect other people,

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.690
if I was careless like that.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.273
And mess up their lives.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.130
It just changes lots of things for me.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:17.693
It makes me a lot more conscious.

00:11:18.653 --> 00:11:20.380
It makes me a better person.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.920
In a way, it's good that I caught HIV,

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:27.920
because I was not really
living, like I tend to live now.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:37.250
I still got to find out how bad
I am, or what strain I have.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:41.606
Those are all things that
I'm waiting for right now.

00:11:41.606 --> 00:11:43.240
I'm a little worried about it because

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.580
there is parts of AIDS
that is pretty strong,

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.930
and they can kill me.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.070
And then maybe I won't
have all the opportunities

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:52.380
that I'm talking about.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.330
But I feel hopeful.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.211
I feel strong.

00:11:57.211 --> 00:11:58.568
- [Mark] You look great.

00:11:58.568 --> 00:12:00.682
You'd never know you're
sick with anything.

00:12:00.682 --> 00:12:02.203
- I don't feel sick at all.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.883
I feel optimistic.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.780
I feel a little bad about my girlfriend,

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:13.800
because she's had a messed up life.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:14.710
I feel bad for her.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.930
She didn't have the
examples that I had in life.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:18.980
I had a great mother.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:21.900
I had good people in my life

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.190
that taught me the right things,

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:26.410
that enabled me to have the perspective

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:27.660
that I have about things.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.753
Even though I grew up in
a real bad neighborhood.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:34.630
I spent most of my life in prison.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:36.000
I just always had good examples.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.250
I've always been blessed,

00:12:38.352 --> 00:12:39.952
to be surrounded by good people.

00:12:43.385 --> 00:12:44.218
- [Mark] All right, Amado.

00:12:44.218 --> 00:12:45.051
Thank you so much for talking to me,

00:12:45.051 --> 00:12:46.210
and sharing your story.

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.263
- It's my pleasure, I
hope it helps somebody.

00:12:49.126 --> 00:12:49.959
- [Mark] I think it will.

00:12:49.959 --> 00:12:50.792
- [Amado] Thank you.

